  "name": "securing-container-registry-with-harbor",
  "description": "Configures the security features of the Harbor open-source container registry - integrated Trivy scanning, Cosign and Notary content trust policies, project-level RBAC, immutable tag and retention rules, and OIDC authentication - to enforce provenance and block deployment of vulnerable images. Use when deploying or hardening Harbor, or when compliance requires that only signed and scanned images can be pulled. Keywords: Harbor, project policy, content trust, immutable tag, retention, robot account, OIDC, replication. Do not use for signing images with Cosign outside a registry - use implementing-image-provenance-verification-with-cosign.",
